(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[18] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"संन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम् ।\nत्यागस्य च हृषीकेश पृथक्केशिनिषूदन ॥","iast":"saṃnyāsasya mahābāho tattvamicchāmi veditum |\ntyāgasya ca hṛṣīkeśa pṛthakkeśiniṣūdana ||","read":"samnyaasasya mahaabaaho tattvamichchhaami veditum |\ntyaagasya cha hrisheekesha prithakkeshinishoodana ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: I desire, O mighty-armed, to know severally the essence of renunciation, O Hrishîkesha, and of relinquishment, O Keshinishûdana.","en2":"I desire to know severally, O mighty-armed, the truth of Sannyâsa, O Hrishikesha, as also of Tyâga, O slayer of Keshi.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"काम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं प्राहुस्त्यागं विचक्षणाः ॥","iast":"kāmyānāṃ karmaṇāṃ nyāsaṃ saṃnyāsaṃ kavayo viduḥ |\nsarvakarmaphalatyāgaṃ prāhustyāgaṃ vicakṣaṇāḥ ||","read":"kaamyaanaam karmanaam nyaasam samnyaasam kavayo viduh |\nsarvakarmaphalatyaagam praahustyaagam vichakshanaah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Sages have known as renunciation the renouncing of works with desire; the relinquishing of the fruit of all actions is called relinquishment by the wise.","en2":"The renunciation of Kâmya actions, the sages understand as. Sannyâsa: the wise declare the abandonment of the fruits of all works as Tyâga.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"त्याज्यं दोषवदित्येके कर्म प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nयज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यमिति चापरे ॥","iast":"tyājyaṃ doṣavadityeke karma prāhurmanīṣiṇaḥ |\nyajñadānatapaḥkarma na tyājyamiti cāpare ||","read":"tyaajyam doshavadityeke karma praahurmaneeshinah |\nyajnadaanatapahkarma na tyaajyamiti chaapare ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"Action should be relinquished as an evil,\" declare some thoughtful men; \"acts of sacrifice, gift and austerity should not be relinquished,\" say others.","en2":"Some philosophers declare that all action should be relinquished as an evil, whilst others (say) that the work of Yajna, gift and austerity should not be relinquished.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"निश्चयं शृणु मे तत्र त्यागे भरतसत्तम ।\nत्यागो हि पुरुषव्याघ्र त्रिविधः सम्प्रकीर्तितः ॥","iast":"niścayaṃ śṛṇu me tatra tyāge bharatasattama |\ntyāgo hi puruṣavyāghra trividhaḥ samprakīrtitaḥ ||","read":"nishchayam shrinu me tatra tyaage bharatasattama |\ntyaago hi purushavyaaghra trividhah samprakeertitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Hear my conclusions as to that relinquishment, O best of the Bhâratas; since relinquishment, O tiger of men, has been explained as threefold.","en2":"Hear from Me the final truth about relinquishment, O best of the Bhâratas. For relinquishment has been declared to be of three kinds, O tiger among men.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यं कार्यमेव तत् ।\nयज्ञो दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम् ॥","iast":"yajñadānatapaḥkarma na tyājyaṃ kāryameva tat |\nyajño dānaṃ tapaścaiva pāvanāni manīṣiṇām ||","read":"yajnadaanatapahkarma na tyaajyam kaaryameva tat |\nyajno daanam tapashchaiva paavanaani maneeshinaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Acts of sacrifice, gift and austerity should not be relinquished, but should be performed; sacrifice, gift and also austerity are the purifiers of the intelligent.","en2":"The work of Yajna, gift and austerity should not be relinquished, but it should indeed be performed; (for) Yajna, gift and austerity are purifying to the wise.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एतान्यपि तु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलानि च ।\nकर्तव्यानीति मे पार्थ निश्चितं मतमुत्तमम् ॥","iast":"etānyapi tu karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā phalāni ca |\nkartavyānīti me pārtha niścitaṃ matamuttamam ||","read":"etaanyapi tu karmaani sangam tyaktvaa phalaani cha |\nkartavyaaneeti me paartha nishchitam matamuttamam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But even these actions should be done leaving aside attachment and fruit, O Pârtha; that is my certain and best belief.","en2":"But even these works, O Pârtha, should be performed, leaving attachment and the fruits;—such is My best and certain conviction.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नियतस्य तु संन्यासः कर्मणो नोपपद्यते ।\nमोहात्तस्य परित्यागस्तामसः परिकीर्तितः ॥","iast":"niyatasya tu saṃnyāsaḥ karmaṇo nopapadyate |\nmohāttasya parityāgastāmasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ ||","read":"niyatasya tu samnyaasah karmano nopapadyate |\nmohaattasya parityaagastaamasah parikeertitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Verily renunciation of actions that are prescribed is not proper; the relinquishment thereof from delusion is said to be of darkness.","en2":"But the renunciation of obligatory action is not proper. Abandonment of the same from delusion is declared to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दुःखमित्येव यत्कर्म कायक्लेशभयात्त्यजेत् ।\nस कृत्वा राजसं त्यागं नैव त्यागफलं लभेत् ॥","iast":"duḥkhamityeva yatkarma kāyakleśabhayāttyajet |\nsa kṛtvā rājasaṃ tyāgaṃ naiva tyāgaphalaṃ labhet ||","read":"duhkhamityeva yatkarma kaayakleshabhayaattyajet |\nsa kritvaa raajasam tyaagam naiva tyaagaphalam labhet ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who relinquisheth an action from fear of physical suffering, saying \"Painful,\" thus performing a passionate relinquishment, obtaineth not the fruit of relinquishment.","en2":"He who from fear of bodily trouble relinquishes action, because it is painful, thus performing a Râjasika relinquishment, he obtains not the fruit thereof.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कार्यमित्येव यत्कर्म नियतं क्रियतेऽर्जुन ।\nसङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलं चैव स त्यागः सात्त्विको मतः ॥","iast":"kāryamityeva yatkarma niyataṃ kriyate’rjuna |\nsaṅgaṃ tyaktvā phalaṃ caiva sa tyāgaḥ sāttviko mataḥ ||","read":"kaaryamityeva yatkarma niyatam kriyate'rjuna |\nsangam tyaktvaa phalam chaiva sa tyaagah saattviko matah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who performeth a prescribed action, saying, \"it ought to be done,\" O Arjuna, relinquishing attachment and also fruit, that relinquishment is regarded as pure.","en2":"When obligatory work is performed, O Arjuna, only because it ought to be done, leaving attachment and fruit, such relinquishment is regarded as Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न द्वेष्ट्यकुशलं कर्म कुशले नानुषज्जते ।\nत्यागी सत्त्वसमाविष्टो मेधावी छिन्नसंशयः ॥","iast":"na dveṣṭyakuśalaṃ karma kuśale nānuṣajjate |\ntyāgī sattvasamāviṣṭo medhāvī chinnasaṃśayaḥ ||","read":"na dveshtyakushalam karma kushale naanushajjate |\ntyaagee sattvasamaavishto medhaavee chhinnasamshayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The relinquisher pervaded by purity, intelligent and with doubts cut away, hateth not unpleasurable action nor is attached to pleasurable.","en2":"The relinquisher endued with Sattva and a steady understanding and with his doubts dispelled, hates not a disagreeable work nor is attached to an agreeable one.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न हि देहभृता शक्यं त्यक्तुं कर्माण्यशेषतः ।\nयस्तु कर्मफलत्यागी स त्यागीत्यभिधीयते ॥","iast":"na hi dehabhṛtā śakyaṃ tyaktuṃ karmāṇyaśeṣataḥ |\nyastu karmaphalatyāgī sa tyāgītyabhidhīyate ||","read":"na hi dehabhritaa shakyam tyaktum karmaanyasheshatah |\nyastu karmaphalatyaagee sa tyaageetyabhidheeyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor indeed can embodied beings completely relinquish action; verily he who relinquisheth the fruit of action, he is said to be a relinquisher.","en2":"Actions cannot be entirely relinquished by an embodied being, but he who relinquishes the fruits of action is called a relinquisher.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनिष्टमिष्टं मिश्रं च त्रिविधं कर्मणः फलम् ।\nभवत्यत्यागिनां प्रेत्य न तु संन्यासिनां क्वचित् ॥","iast":"aniṣṭamiṣṭaṃ miśraṃ ca trividhaṃ karmaṇaḥ phalam |\nbhavatyatyāgināṃ pretya na tu saṃnyāsināṃ kvacit ||","read":"anishtamishtam mishram cha trividham karmanah phalam |\nbhavatyatyaaginaam pretya na tu samnyaasinaam kvachit ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Good, evil and mixed—threefold is the fruit of action hereafter for the non-relinquisher; but there is none ever for the renouncer.","en2":"The threefold fruit of action—disagreeable, agreeable and mixed,—accrues to non-relinquishers after death, but never to relinquishers.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पञ्चैतानि महाबाहो कारणानि निबोध मे ।\nसांख्ये कृतान्ते प्रोक्तानि सिद्धये सर्वकर्मणाम् ॥","iast":"pañcaitāni mahābāho kāraṇāni nibodha me |\nsāṃkhye kṛtānte proktāni siddhaye sarvakarmaṇām ||","read":"panchaitaani mahaabaaho kaaranaani nibodha me |\nsaamkhye kritaante proktaani siddhaye sarvakarmanaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"These five causes, O mighty-armed, learn of Me as declared in the Sâñkhya system for the accomplishment of all actions:","en2":"Learn from Me, O mighty-armed, these five causes for the accomplishment of all works as declared in the wisdom which is the end of all action:","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अधिष्ठानं तथा कर्ता करणं च पृथग्विधम् ।\nविविधाश्च पृथक्चेष्टा दैवं चैवात्र पञ्चमम् ॥","iast":"adhiṣṭhānaṃ tathā kartā karaṇaṃ ca pṛthagvidham |\nvividhāśca pṛthakceṣṭā daivaṃ caivātra pañcamam ||","read":"adhishthaanam tathaa kartaa karanam cha prithagvidham |\nvividhaashcha prithakcheshtaa daivam chaivaatra panchamam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The body, the actor, the various organs, the diverse kinds of energies, and the presiding deities also, the fifth.","en2":"The body, the agent, the various senses, the different functions of a manifold kind, and the presiding divinity, the fifth of these;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शरीरवाङ्मनोभिर्यत्कर्म प्रारभते नरः ।\nन्याय्यं वा विपरीतं वा पञ्चैते तस्य हेतवः ॥","iast":"śarīravāṅmanobhiryatkarma prārabhate naraḥ |\nnyāyyaṃ vā viparītaṃ vā pañcaite tasya hetavaḥ ||","read":"shareeravaanmanobhiryatkarma praarabhate narah |\nnyaayyam vaa vipareetam vaa panchaite tasya hetavah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatever action a man performeth by his body, speech and mind, whether right or the reverse, these five are the cause thereof.","en2":"Whatever action a man performs by his body, speech and mind—whether right or the reverse—these five are its causes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्रैवं सति कर्तारमात्मानं केवलं तु यः ।\nपश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति दुर्मतिः ॥","iast":"tatraivaṃ sati kartāramātmānaṃ kevalaṃ tu yaḥ |\npaśyatyakṛtabuddhitvānna sa paśyati durmatiḥ ||","read":"tatraivam sati kartaaramaatmaanam kevalam tu yah |\npashyatyakritabuddhitvaanna sa pashyati durmatih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That being so, he verily who—owing to untrained Reason—looketh on his Self, which is isolated, as the actor, he of perverted intelligence, seeth not.","en2":"Such being the case, he who through a non-purified understanding looks upon his Self, the Absolute, as the agent, he of perverted mind sees not.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्य नाहंकृतो भावो बुद्धिर्यस्य न लिप्यते ।\nहत्वापि स इमाँल्लोकान्न हन्ति न निबध्यते ॥","iast":"yasya nāhaṃkṛto bhāvo buddhiryasya na lipyate |\nhatvāpi sa imām̐llokānna hanti na nibadhyate ||","read":"yasya naahamkrito bhaavo buddhiryasya na lipyate |\nhatvaapi sa imaanllokaanna hanti na nibadhyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who is free from the egoistic notion, whose Reason is not affected, though he slay these peoples, he slayeth not, nor is bound.","en2":"He who is free from the notion of egoism, whose intelligence is not affected (by good or evil), though he kills these people, he kills not, nor is bound (by the action);","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं परिज्ञाता त्रिविधा कर्मचोदना ।\nकरणं कर्म कर्तेति त्रिविधः कर्मसंग्रहः ॥","iast":"jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ parijñātā trividhā karmacodanā |\nkaraṇaṃ karma karteti trividhaḥ karmasaṃgrahaḥ ||","read":"jnaanam jneyam parijnaataa trividhaa karmachodanaa |\nkaranam karma karteti trividhah karmasamgrahah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Knowledge, the knowable and the knower, the threefold impulse to action; the organ, the action, the actor, the threefold constituents of action.","en2":"Knowledge, the known and the knower form the threefold cause of action. The instrument, the object and the agent are the threefold basis of action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानं कर्म च कर्ता च त्रिधैव गुणभेदतः ।\nप्रोच्यते गुणसंख्याने यथावच्छृणु तान्यपि ॥","iast":"jñānaṃ karma ca kartā ca tridhaiva guṇabhedataḥ |\nprocyate guṇasaṃkhyāne yathāvacchṛṇu tānyapi ||","read":"jnaanam karma cha kartaa cha tridhaiva gunabhedatah |\nprochyate gunasamkhyaane yathaavachchhrinu taanyapi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Knowledge, action and actor in the category of qualities are also said to be severally threefold, from the difference of qualities; hear thou duly these also.","en2":"Knowledge, action and agent are declared in the Sânkhya philosophy to be of three kinds only, from the distinction of Gunas: hear them also duly.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वभूतेषु येनैकं भावमव्ययमीक्षते ।\nअविभक्तं विभक्तेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि सात्त्विकम् ॥","iast":"sarvabhūteṣu yenaikaṃ bhāvamavyayamīkṣate |\navibhaktaṃ vibhakteṣu tajjñānaṃ viddhi sāttvikam ||","read":"sarvabhooteshu yenaikam bhaavamavyayameekshate |\navibhaktam vibhakteshu tajjnaanam viddhi saattvikam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That by which one indestructible Being is seen in all beings, inseparate in the separated, know thou that knowledge as pure.","en2":"That by which the one indestructible Substance is seen in all beings, inseparate in the separated, know that knowledge to be Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पृथक्त्वेन तु यज्ज्ञानं नानाभावान्पृथग्विधान् ।\nवेत्ति सर्वेषु भूतेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि राजसम् ॥","iast":"pṛthaktvena tu yajjñānaṃ nānābhāvānpṛthagvidhān |\nvetti sarveṣu bhūteṣu tajjñānaṃ viddhi rājasam ||","read":"prithaktvena tu yajjnaanam naanaabhaavaanprithagvidhaan |\nvetti sarveshu bhooteshu tajjnaanam viddhi raajasam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But that knowledge which regardeth the several manifold existences in all beings as separate, that knowledge know thou as of passion;","en2":"But that knowledge which sees in all beings various entities of distinct kinds as different from one another, know thou that knowledge as Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्तु कृत्स्नवदेकस्मिन्कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम् ।\nअतत्त्वार्थवदल्पं च तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"yattu kṛtsnavadekasminkārye saktamahaitukam |\natattvārthavadalpaṃ ca tattāmasamudāhṛtam ||","read":"yattu kritsnavadekasminkaarye saktamahaitukam |\natattvaarthavadalpam cha tattaamasamudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"While that which clingeth to each one thing as if it were the whole, without reason, without grasping the reality, narrow, that is declared to be dark.","en2":"Whilst that which is confined to one single effect as if it were the whole, without reason, without foundation in truth, and trivial,—that is declared to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नियतं सङ्गरहितमरागद्वेषतः कृतम् ।\nअफलप्रेप्सुना कर्म यत्तत्सात्त्विकमुच्यते ॥","iast":"niyataṃ saṅgarahitamarāgadveṣataḥ kṛtam |\naphalaprepsunā karma yattatsāttvikamucyate ||","read":"niyatam sangarahitamaraagadveshatah kritam |\naphalaprepsunaa karma yattatsaattvikamuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"An action which is ordained, done by one undesirous of fruit, devoid of attachment, without love or hate, that is called pure.","en2":"An ordained action done without love or hatred by one not desirous of the fruit and free from attachment, is declared to be Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्तु कामेप्सुना कर्म साहङ्कारेण वा पुनः ।\nक्रियते बहुलायासं तद्राजसमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"yattu kāmepsunā karma sāhaṅkāreṇa vā punaḥ |\nkriyate bahulāyāsaṃ tadrājasamudāhṛtam ||","read":"yattu kaamepsunaa karma saahankaarena vaa punah |\nkriyate bahulaayaasam tadraajasamudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But that action that is done by one longing for desires, or again with egoism, or with much effort, that is declared to be passionate.","en2":"But the action which is performed desiring desires, or with self-conceit and with much effort, is declared to be Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनुबन्धं क्षयं हिंसामनपेक्ष्य च पौरुषम् ।\nमोहादारभ्यते कर्म यत्तत्तामसमुच्यते ॥","iast":"anubandhaṃ kṣayaṃ hiṃsāmanapekṣya ca pauruṣam |\nmohādārabhyate karma yattattāmasamucyate ||","read":"anubandham kshayam himsaamanapekshya cha paurusham |\nmohaadaarabhyate karma yattattaamasamuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The action undertaken from delusion, without regard to capacity and consequences—loss and injury to others—that is declared to be dark.","en2":"That action is declared to be Tâmasika which is undertaken through delusion, without heed to the consequence, loss (of power and wealth), injury (to others) and (one's own) ability.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योर्निर्विकारः कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते ॥","iast":"muktasaṅgo’nahaṃvādī dhṛtyutsāhasamanvitaḥ |\nsiddhyasiddhyornirvikāraḥ kartā sāttvika ucyate ||","read":"muktasango'nahamvaadee dhrityutsaahasamanvitah |\nsiddhyasiddhyornirvikaarah kartaa saattvika uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Liberated from attachment, not egoistic, endued with firmness and confidence, unchanged by success or failure, that actor is called pure.","en2":"An agent who is free from attachment, non-egotistic, endued with fortitude and enthusiasm and unaffected in success or failure, is called Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रागी कर्मफलप्रेप्सुर्लुब्धो हिंसात्मकोऽशुचिः ।\nहर्षशोकान्वितः कर्ता राजसः परिकीर्तितः ॥","iast":"rāgī karmaphalaprepsurlubdho hiṃsātmako’śuciḥ |\nharṣaśokānvitaḥ kartā rājasaḥ parikīrtitaḥ ||","read":"raagee karmaphalaprepsurlubdho himsaatmako'shuchih |\nharshashokaanvitah kartaa raajasah parikeertitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Impassioned, desiring to obtain the fruit of actions, greedy, harmful, impure, moved by joy and sorrow, such an actor is pronounced passionate.","en2":"He who is passionate, desirous of the fruits of action, greedy, malignant, impure, easily elated or dejected, such an agent is called Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अयुक्तः प्राकृतः स्तब्धः शठो नैष्कृतिकोऽलसः ।\nविषादी दीर्घसूत्री च कर्ता तामस उच्यते ॥","iast":"ayuktaḥ prākṛtaḥ stabdhaḥ śaṭho naiṣkṛtiko’lasaḥ |\nviṣādī dīrghasūtrī ca kartā tāmasa ucyate ||","read":"ayuktah praakritah stabdhah shatho naishkritiko'lasah |\nvishaadee deerghasootree cha kartaa taamasa uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Discordant, vulgar, stubborn, cheating, malicious, indolent, despairful, procrastinating, that actor is called dark.","en2":"Unsteady, vulgar, arrogant, dishonest, malicious, indolent, desponding and procrastinating, such an agent is called Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बुद्धेर्भेदं धृतेश्चैव गुणतस्त्रिविधं शृणु ।\nप्रोच्यमानमशेषेण पृथक्त्वेन धनञ्जय ॥","iast":"buddherbhedaṃ dhṛteścaiva guṇatastrividhaṃ śṛṇu |\nprocyamānamaśeṣeṇa pṛthaktvena dhanañjaya ||","read":"buddherbhedam dhriteshchaiva gunatastrividham shrinu |\nprochyamaanamasheshena prithaktvena dhananjaya ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The division of Reason and of firmness also, threefold according to the qualities, hear thou related, unreservedly and severally, O Dhananjaya.","en2":"Hear thou the triple distinction of intellect and fortitude, according to the Gunas, as I declare them exhaustively and severally, O Dhananjaya.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कार्याकार्ये भयाभये ।\nबन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी ॥","iast":"pravṛttiṃ ca nivṛttiṃ ca kāryākārye bhayābhaye |\nbandhaṃ mokṣaṃ ca yā vetti buddhiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī ||","read":"pravrittim cha nivrittim cha kaaryaakaarye bhayaabhaye |\nbandham moksham cha yaa vetti buddhih saa paartha saattvikee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which knoweth energy and abstinence, what ought to be done and what ought not to be done, fear and fearlessness, bondage and liberation, that Reason is pure, O Pârtha.","en2":"That which knows the paths of work and renunciation, right and wrong action, fear and fearlessness, bondage and liberation, that intellect, O Pârtha, is Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यया धर्ममधर्मं च कार्यं चाकार्यमेव च ।\nअयथावत्प्रजानाति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ राजसी ॥","iast":"yayā dharmamadharmaṃ ca kāryaṃ cākāryameva ca |\nayathāvatprajānāti buddhiḥ sā pārtha rājasī ||","read":"yayaa dharmamadharmam cha kaaryam chaakaaryameva cha |\nayathaavatprajaanaati buddhih saa paartha raajasee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That by which one understandeth away Right and Wrong and also what ought to be done and what ought not to be done, that Reason, O Pârtha, is passionate.","en2":"That which has a distorted apprehension of Dharma and its opposite and also of right action and its opposite, that intellect, O Pârtha, is Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अधर्मं धर्ममिति या मन्यते तमसाऽऽवृता ।\nसर्वार्थान्विपरीतांश्च बुद्धिः सा पार्थ तामसी ॥","iast":"adharmaṃ dharmamiti yā manyate tamasā’’vṛtā |\nsarvārthānviparītāṃśca buddhiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī ||","read":"adharmam dharmamiti yaa manyate tamasaa''vritaa |\nsarvaarthaanvipareetaamshcha buddhih saa paartha taamasee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which, enwrapped in darkness, thinketh wrong to be right and seeth all things subverted, that Reason, O Pârtha, is of darkness.","en2":"That which enveloped in darkness regards Adharma as Dharma and views all things in a perverted light, that intellect, O Pârtha, is Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"धृत्या यया धारयते मनःप्राणेन्द्रियक्रियाः ।\nयोगेनाव्यभिचारिण्या धृतिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी ॥","iast":"dhṛtyā yayā dhārayate manaḥprāṇendriyakriyāḥ |\nyogenāvyabhicāriṇyā dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha sāttvikī ||","read":"dhrityaa yayaa dhaarayate manahpraanendriyakriyaah |\nyogenaavyabhichaarinyaa dhritih saa paartha saattvikee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The unwavering firmness by which, through Yoga, one restraineth the activity of the mind, of the life breaths and of the sense-organs, that firmness, O Pârtha, is pure.","en2":"The fortitude by which the functions of the mind, the Prâna and the senses, O Pârtha, are regulated, that fortitude, unswerving through Yoga, is Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यया तु धर्मकामार्थान् धृत्या धारयतेऽर्जुन ।\nप्रसङ्गेन फलाकाङ्क्षी धृतिः सा पार्थ राजसी ॥","iast":"yayā tu dharmakāmārthān dhṛtyā dhārayate’rjuna |\nprasaṅgena phalākāṅkṣī dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha rājasī ||","read":"yayaa tu dharmakaamaarthaan dhrityaa dhaarayate'rjuna |\nprasangena phalaakaankshee dhritih saa paartha raajasee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But the firmness, O Arjuna, by which, from attachment desirous of fruit, one holdeth fast duty, desire and wealth, that firmness, O Pârtha, is passionate.","en2":"But the fortitude by which one regulates (one's mind) to Dharma, desire and wealth, desirous of the fruit of each from attachment, that fortitude, O Pârtha, is Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यया स्वप्नं भयं शोकं विषादं मदमेव च ।\nन विमुञ्चति दुर्मेधा धृतिः सा पार्थ तामसी ॥","iast":"yayā svapnaṃ bhayaṃ śokaṃ viṣādaṃ madameva ca |\nna vimuñcati durmedhā dhṛtiḥ sā pārtha tāmasī ||","read":"yayaa svapnam bhayam shokam vishaadam madameva cha |\nna vimunchati durmedhaa dhritih saa paartha taamasee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That by which one from stupidity doth not abandon sleep, fear, grief, despair, and also vanity, that firmness, O Pârtha, is dark.","en2":"That by which a stupid man does not give up sleep, fear, grief, despondency and also overweening conceit, that fortitude, O Pârtha, is Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":36,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सुखं त्विदानीं त्रिविधं शृणु मे भरतर्षभ ।\nअभ्यासाद्रमते यत्र दुःखान्तं च निगच्छति ॥","iast":"sukhaṃ tvidānīṃ trividhaṃ śṛṇu me bharatarṣabha |\nabhyāsādramate yatra duḥkhāntaṃ ca nigacchati ||","read":"sukham tvidaaneem trividham shrinu me bharatarshabha |\nabhyaasaadramate yatra duhkhaantam cha nigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And now the threefold kinds of pleasure hear thou from Me, O bull of the Bhâratas. That in which one by practice rejoiceth, and which putteth an end to pain;","en2":"And now hear from Me, O bull of the Bhâratas, of the threefold happiness. That happiness which one learns to enjoy by habit, and by which one comes to the end of pain;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":37,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्तदग्रे विषमिव परिणामेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nतत्सुखं सात्त्विकं प्रोक्तमात्मबुद्धिप्रसादजम् ॥","iast":"yattadagre viṣamiva pariṇāme’mṛtopamam |\ntatsukhaṃ sāttvikaṃ proktamātmabuddhiprasādajam ||","read":"yattadagre vishamiva parinaame'mritopamam |\ntatsukham saattvikam proktamaatmabuddhiprasaadajam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Which at first is as venom but in the end is as nectar; that pleasure is said to be pure, born of the blissful knowledge of the Self.","en2":"That which is like poison at first, but like nectar at the end; that happiness is declared to be Sâttvika, born of the translucence of intellect due to Self-realisation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":38,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विषयेन्द्रियसंयोगाद्यत्तदग्रेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nपरिणामे विषमिव तत्सुखं राजसं स्मृतम् ॥","iast":"viṣayendriyasaṃyogādyattadagre’mṛtopamam |\npariṇāme viṣamiva tatsukhaṃ rājasaṃ smṛtam ||","read":"vishayendriyasamyogaadyattadagre'mritopamam |\nparinaame vishamiva tatsukham raajasam smritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which from the union of the senses with their objects at first is as nectar, but in the end is like venom, that pleasure is accounted passionate.","en2":"That which arises from the contact of object with sense, at first like nectar, but at the end like poison, that happiness is declared to be Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":39,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदग्रे चानुबन्धे च सुखं मोहनमात्मनः ।\nनिद्रालस्यप्रमादोत्थं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"yadagre cānubandhe ca sukhaṃ mohanamātmanaḥ |\nnidrālasyapramādotthaṃ tattāmasamudāhṛtam ||","read":"yadagre chaanubandhe cha sukham mohanamaatmanah |\nnidraalasyapramaadottham tattaamasamudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That pleasure which both at first and afterwards is delusive of the self, arising from sleep, indolence and heedlessness, that is declared dark.","en2":"That happiness which begins and results in self-delusion arising from sleep, indolence and miscomprehension, that is declared to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न तदस्ति पृथिव्यां वा दिवि देवेषु वा पुनः ।\nसत्त्वं प्रकृतिजैर्मुक्तं यदेभिः स्यात्त्रिभिर्गुणैः ॥","iast":"na tadasti pṛthivyāṃ vā divi deveṣu vā punaḥ |\nsattvaṃ prakṛtijairmuktaṃ yadebhiḥ syāttribhirguṇaiḥ ||","read":"na tadasti prithivyaam vaa divi deveshu vaa punah |\nsattvam prakritijairmuktam yadebhih syaattribhirgunaih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There is not an entity, either on the earth or again in heaven among the Shining Ones, that is liberated from these three qualities, born of Matter.","en2":"There is no entity on earth, or again in heaven among the Devas, that is devoid of these three Gunas, born of Prakriti.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशां शूद्राणां च परंतप ।\nकर्माणि प्रविभक्तानि स्वभावप्रभवैर्गुणैः ॥","iast":"brāhmaṇakṣatriyaviśāṃ śūdrāṇāṃ ca paraṃtapa |\nkarmāṇi pravibhaktāni svabhāvaprabhavairguṇaiḥ ||","read":"braahmanakshatriyavishaam shoodraanaam cha paramtapa |\nkarmaani pravibhaktaani svabhaavaprabhavairgunaih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of Brâhmanas, Kshattriyas, Vaishyas and Shûdras, O Parantapa, the duties have been distributed, according to the qualities born of their own natures.","en2":"Of Brâhmanas and Kshatriyas and Vaishyas, as also of Sudras, O scorcher of foes, the duties are distributed according to the Gunas born of their own nature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शमो दमस्तपः शौचं क्षान्तिरार्जवमेव च ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यं ब्रह्मकर्म स्वभावजम् ॥","iast":"śamo damastapaḥ śaucaṃ kṣāntirārjavameva ca |\njñānaṃ vijñānamāstikyaṃ brahmakarma svabhāvajam ||","read":"shamo damastapah shaucham kshaantiraarjavameva cha |\njnaanam vijnaanamaastikyam brahmakarma svabhaavajam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Serenity, self-restraint, austerity, purity, forgiveness and also uprightness, wisdom, knowledge, belief in God, are the Brâhmana duty, born of his own nature.","en2":"The control of the mind and the senses, austerity, purity, forbearance, and also uprightness, knowledge, realisation, belief in a hereafter,—these are the duties of the Brâhmanas, born of (their own) nature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":43,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शौर्यं तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनम् ।\nदानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं कर्म स्वभावजम् ॥","iast":"śauryaṃ tejo dhṛtirdākṣyaṃ yuddhe cāpyapalāyanam |\ndānamīśvarabhāvaśca kṣātraṃ karma svabhāvajam ||","read":"shauryam tejo dhritirdaakshyam yuddhe chaapyapalaayanam |\ndaanameeshvarabhaavashcha kshaatram karma svabhaavajam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Prowess, splendour, firmness, dexterity, and also not flying from battle, generosity, the nature of a ruler, are the Kshattriya duty, born of his own nature.","en2":"Prowess, boldness, fortitude, dexterity, and also not flying from battle, generosity and sovereignty are the duties of the Kshatriyas, born of (their own) nature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":44,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कृषिगौरक्ष्यवाणिज्यं वैश्यकर्म स्वभावजम् ।\nपरिचर्यात्मकं कर्म शूद्रस्यापि स्वभावजम् ॥","iast":"kṛṣigaurakṣyavāṇijyaṃ vaiśyakarma svabhāvajam |\nparicaryātmakaṃ karma śūdrasyāpi svabhāvajam ||","read":"krishigaurakshyavaanijyam vaishyakarma svabhaavajam |\nparicharyaatmakam karma shoodrasyaapi svabhaavajam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Ploughing, protection of kine, and trade are the Vaishya duty, born of his own nature. Action of the nature of service is the Shûdra duty, born of his own nature.","en2":"Agriculture, cattle-rearing and trade are the duties of the Vaishyas, born of (their own) nature; and action consisting of service is the duty of the Sudras, born of (their own) nature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":45,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः ।\nस्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु ॥","iast":"sve sve karmaṇyabhirataḥ saṃsiddhiṃ labhate naraḥ |\nsvakarmanirataḥ siddhiṃ yathā vindati tacchṛṇu ||","read":"sve sve karmanyabhiratah samsiddhim labhate narah |\nsvakarmaniratah siddhim yathaa vindati tachchhrinu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Man reacheth perfection by each being intent on his own duty. Listen thou how perfection is won by him who is intent on his own duty.","en2":"Devoted each to his own duty, man attains the highest perfection. How engaged in his own duty, he attains perfection, that hear.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":46,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यतः प्रवृत्तिर्भूतानां येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nस्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः ॥","iast":"yataḥ pravṛttirbhūtānāṃ yena sarvamidaṃ tatam |\nsvakarmaṇā tamabhyarcya siddhiṃ vindati mānavaḥ ||","read":"yatah pravrittirbhootaanaam yena sarvamidam tatam |\nsvakarmanaa tamabhyarchya siddhim vindati maanavah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He from whom is the emanation of beings, by Whom all This is pervaded, by worshipping Him in his own duty a man winneth perfection.","en2":"From whom is the evolution of all beings, by whom all this is pervaded, worshipping Him with his own duty, a man attains perfection.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":47,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वभावनियतं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम् ॥","iast":"śreyānsvadharmo viguṇaḥ paradharmātsvanuṣṭhitāt |\nsvabhāvaniyataṃ karma kurvannāpnoti kilbiṣam ||","read":"shreyaansvadharmo vigunah paradharmaatsvanushthitaat |\nsvabhaavaniyatam karma kurvannaapnoti kilbisham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Better is one's own duty though destitute of merits than the well-executed duty of another. He who doeth the duty laid down by his own nature incurreth not sin.","en2":"Better is one's own Dharma, (though) imperfect, than the Dharma of another well-performed. He who does the duty ordained by his own nature incurs no evil.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":48,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सहजं कर्म कौन्तेय सदोषमपि न त्यजेत् ।\nसर्वारम्भा हि दोषेण धूमेनाग्निरिवावृताः ॥","iast":"sahajaṃ karma kaunteya sadoṣamapi na tyajet |\nsarvārambhā hi doṣeṇa dhūmenāgnirivāvṛtāḥ ||","read":"sahajam karma kaunteya sadoshamapi na tyajet |\nsarvaarambhaa hi doshena dhoomenaagnirivaavritaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Congenital duty, O son of Kunti, though defective, ought not to be abandoned. All undertakings indeed are clouded by defects as fire by smoke.","en2":"One should not relinquish, O son of Kunti, the duty to which one is born, though it is attended with evil; for, all undertakings are enveloped by evil, as fire by smoke.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":49,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"असक्तबुद्धिः सर्वत्र जितात्मा विगतस्पृहः ।\nनैष्कर्म्यसिद्धिं परमां संन्यासेनाधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"asaktabuddhiḥ sarvatra jitātmā vigataspṛhaḥ |\nnaiṣkarmyasiddhiṃ paramāṃ saṃnyāsenādhigacchati ||","read":"asaktabuddhih sarvatra jitaatmaa vigatasprihah |\nnaishkarmyasiddhim paramaam samnyaasenaadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He whose Reason is everywhere unattached, the self-subdued, dead to desires, he goeth by renunciation to the supreme perfection of freedom from obligation.","en2":"He whose intellect is unattached everywhere, who has subdued his heart, whose desires have fled, he attains by renunciation to the supreme perfection, consisting of freedom from action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":50,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सिद्धिं प्राप्तो यथा ब्रह्म तथाप्नोति निबोध मे ।\nसमासेनैव कौन्तेय निष्ठा ज्ञानस्य या परा ॥","iast":"siddhiṃ prāpto yathā brahma tathāpnoti nibodha me |\nsamāsenaiva kaunteya niṣṭhā jñānasya yā parā ||","read":"siddhim praapto yathaa brahma tathaapnoti nibodha me |\nsamaasenaiva kaunteya nishthaa jnaanasya yaa paraa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"How he who hath attained perfection obtaineth the Eternal, that highest state of wisdom, learn thou from Me only succinctly, O Kaunteya.","en2":"Learn from Me in brief, O son of Kunti, how reaching such perfection, he attains to Brahman, that supreme consummation of knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":51,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बुद्ध्या विशुद्धया युक्तो धृत्याऽऽत्मानं नियम्य च ।\nशब्दादीन् विषयांस्त्यक्त्वा रागद्वेषौ व्युदस्य च ॥","iast":"buddhyā viśuddhayā yukto dhṛtyā’’tmānaṃ niyamya ca |\nśabdādīn viṣayāṃstyaktvā rāgadveṣau vyudasya ca ||","read":"buddhyaa vishuddhayaa yukto dhrityaa''tmaanam niyamya cha |\nshabdaadeen vishayaamstyaktvaa raagadveshau vyudasya cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"United to this Reason, purified, controlling the self by firmness, having abandoned sound and the other objects of the senses, having laid aside passion and malice,","en2":"Endued with a pure intellect, subduing the body and the senses with fortitude, relinquishing sound and such other sense-objects, abandoning attraction and hatred;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":52,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विविक्तसेवी लघ्वाशी यतवाक्कायमानसः ।\nध्यानयोगपरो नित्यं वैराग्यं समुपाश्रितः ॥","iast":"viviktasevī laghvāśī yatavākkāyamānasaḥ |\ndhyānayogaparo nityaṃ vairāgyaṃ samupāśritaḥ ||","read":"viviktasevee laghvaashee yatavaakkaayamaanasah |\ndhyaanayogaparo nityam vairaagyam samupaashritah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Dwelling in solitude, abstemious, speech, body and mind subdued, constantly fixed in meditation and yoga, taking refuge in dispassion,","en2":"Resorting to a sequestered spot, eating but little, body, speech and mind controlled, ever engaged in meditation and concentration, possessed of dispassion;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":53,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहङ्कारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं परिग्रहम् ।\nविमुच्य निर्ममः शान्तो ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥","iast":"ahaṅkāraṃ balaṃ darpaṃ kāmaṃ krodhaṃ parigraham |\nvimucya nirmamaḥ śānto brahmabhūyāya kalpate ||","read":"ahankaaram balam darpam kaamam krodham parigraham |\nvimuchya nirmamah shaanto brahmabhooyaaya kalpate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having cast aside egoism, violence, arrogance, desire, wrath, covetousness, selfless and peaceful—he is fit to become the Eternal.","en2":"Forsaking egoism, power, pride, lust, wrath and property, freed from the notion of \"mine,\" and tranquil, he is fit for becoming Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":54,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ब्रह्मभूतः प्रसन्नात्मा न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nसमः सर्वेषु भूतेषु मद्भक्तिं लभते पराम् ॥","iast":"brahmabhūtaḥ prasannātmā na śocati na kāṅkṣati |\nsamaḥ sarveṣu bhūteṣu madbhaktiṃ labhate parām ||","read":"brahmabhootah prasannaatmaa na shochati na kaankshati |\nsamah sarveshu bhooteshu madbhaktim labhate paraam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Becoming the Eternal, serene in the Self, he neither grieveth nor desireth; the same to all beings, he obtaineth supreme devotion unto Me.","en2":"Brahman-become, tranquil-minded, he neither grieves nor desires; the same to all beings, he attains to supreme devotion unto Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":55,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भक्त्या मामभिजानाति यावान्यश्चास्मि तत्त्वतः ।\nततो मां तत्त्वतो ज्ञात्वा विशते तदनन्तरम् ॥","iast":"bhaktyā māmabhijānāti yāvānyaścāsmi tattvataḥ |\ntato māṃ tattvato jñātvā viśate tadanantaram ||","read":"bhaktyaa maamabhijaanaati yaavaanyashchaasmi tattvatah |\ntato maam tattvato jnaatvaa vishate tadanantaram ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"By devotion he knoweth Me in essence, who and what I am; having thus known Me in essence he forthwith entereth into the Supreme.","en2":"By devotion he knows Me in reality, what and who I am; then having known Me in reality, he forthwith enters into Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":56,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वकर्माण्यपि सदा कुर्वाणो मद्व्यपाश्रयः ।\nमत्प्रसादादवाप्नोति शाश्वतं पदमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"sarvakarmāṇyapi sadā kurvāṇo madvyapāśrayaḥ |\nmatprasādādavāpnoti śāśvataṃ padamavyayam ||","read":"sarvakarmaanyapi sadaa kurvaano madvyapaashrayah |\nmatprasaadaadavaapnoti shaashvatam padamavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Though ever performing all actions, taking refuge in Me, by My grace he obtaineth the eternal indestructible abode.","en2":"Even doing all actions always, taking refuge in Me,—by My grace he attains to the eternal, immutable State.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":57,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"चेतसा सर्वकर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्परः ।\nबुद्धियोगमुपाश्रित्य मच्चित्तः सततं भव ॥","iast":"cetasā sarvakarmāṇi mayi saṃnyasya matparaḥ |\nbuddhiyogamupāśritya maccittaḥ satataṃ bhava ||","read":"chetasaa sarvakarmaani mayi samnyasya matparah |\nbuddhiyogamupaashritya machchittah satatam bhava ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Renouncing mentally all works in Me, intent on Me, resorting to the yoga of discrimination, have thy thought ever on Me.","en2":"Resigning mentally all deeds to Me, having Me as the highest goal, resorting to Buddhi-Yoga do thou ever fix thy mind on Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":58,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि ।\nअथ चेत्त्वमहङ्कारान्न श्रोष्यसि विनङ्क्ष्यसि ॥","iast":"maccittaḥ sarvadurgāṇi matprasādāttariṣyasi |\natha cettvamahaṅkārānna śroṣyasi vinaṅkṣyasi ||","read":"machchittah sarvadurgaani matprasaadaattarishyasi |\natha chettvamahankaaraanna shroshyasi vinankshyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thinking on Me, thou shalt overcome all obstacles by My grace: but if from egoism thou wilt not listen, thou shalt be destroyed utterly.","en2":"Fixing thy mind on Me, thou shalt, by My grace, overcome all obstacles; but if from self-conceit thou wilt not hear Me, thou shalt perish.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":59,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदहङ्कारमाश्रित्य न योत्स्य इति मन्यसे ।\nमिथ्यैष व्यवसायस्ते प्रकृतिस्त्वां नियोक्ष्यति ॥","iast":"yadahaṅkāramāśritya na yotsya iti manyase |\nmithyaiṣa vyavasāyaste prakṛtistvāṃ niyokṣyati ||","read":"yadahankaaramaashritya na yotsya iti manyase |\nmithyaisha vyavasaayaste prakritistvaam niyokshyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Entrenched in egoism, thou thinkest, \"I will not fight;\" to no purpose thy determination; nature will constrain thee.","en2":"If filled with self-conceit thou thinkest, \"I will not fight,\" vain is this thy resolve; thy Prakriti will constrain thee.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":60,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स्वभावजेन कौन्तेय निबद्धः स्वेन कर्मणा ।\nकर्तुं नेच्छसि यन्मोहात्करिष्यस्यवशोऽपि तत् ॥","iast":"svabhāvajena kaunteya nibaddhaḥ svena karmaṇā |\nkartuṃ necchasi yanmohātkariṣyasyavaśo’pi tat ||","read":"svabhaavajena kaunteya nibaddhah svena karmanaa |\nkartum nechchhasi yanmohaatkarishyasyavasho'pi tat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"O son of Kuntî, bound by thine own duty born of thine own nature, that which from delusion thou desirest not to do, even that helplessly thou shalt perform.","en2":"Fettered, O son of Kunti, by thy own Karma, born of thy own nature, what thou, from delusion, desirest not to do, thou shalt have to do in spite of thyself.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":61,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां हृद्देशेऽर्जुन तिष्ठति ।\nभ्रामयन्सर्वभूतानि यन्त्रारूढानि मायया ॥","iast":"īśvaraḥ sarvabhūtānāṃ hṛddeśe’rjuna tiṣṭhati |\nbhrāmayansarvabhūtāni yantrārūḍhāni māyayā ||","read":"eeshvarah sarvabhootaanaam hriddeshe'rjuna tishthati |\nbhraamayansarvabhootaani yantraaroodhaani maayayaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Lord dwelleth in the hearts of all beings, O Arjuna, by His illusive Power causing all beings to revolve, as though mounted on a potter's wheel.","en2":"The Lord, O Arjuna, dwells in the hearts of all beings, causing all beings, by His Mâyâ, to revolve, (as if) mounted on a machine.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":62,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तमेव शरणं गच्छ सर्वभावेन भारत ।\nतत्प्रसादात्परां शान्तिं स्थानं प्राप्स्यसि शाश्वतम् ॥","iast":"tameva śaraṇaṃ gaccha sarvabhāvena bhārata |\ntatprasādātparāṃ śāntiṃ sthānaṃ prāpsyasi śāśvatam ||","read":"tameva sharanam gachchha sarvabhaavena bhaarata |\ntatprasaadaatparaam shaantim sthaanam praapsyasi shaashvatam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Flee unto Him for shelter with all thy being, O Bhârata; by His grace thou shalt obtain supreme peace, the everlasting dwelling-place.","en2":"Take refuge in Him with all thy heart, O Bhârata; by His grace shalt thou attain supreme peace (and) the eternal abode.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":63,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं गुह्याद्गुह्यतरं मया ।\nविमृश्यैतदशेषेण यथेच्छसि तथा कुरु ॥","iast":"iti te jñānamākhyātaṃ guhyādguhyataraṃ mayā |\nvimṛśyaitadaśeṣeṇa yathecchasi tathā kuru ||","read":"iti te jnaanamaakhyaatam guhyaadguhyataram mayaa |\nvimrishyaitadasheshena yathechchhasi tathaa kuru ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thus hath wisdom, more secret than secrecy itself, been declared unto thee by Me; having reflected on it fully, then act thou as thou listest.","en2":"Thus has wisdom more profound than all profundities, been declared to. thee by Me; reflecting over it fully, act as thou likest.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":64,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वगुह्यतमं भूयः शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nइष्टोऽसि मे दृढमिति ततो वक्ष्यामि ते हितम् ॥","iast":"sarvaguhyatamaṃ bhūyaḥ śṛṇu me paramaṃ vacaḥ |\niṣṭo’si me dṛḍhamiti tato vakṣyāmi te hitam ||","read":"sarvaguhyatamam bhooyah shrinu me paramam vachah |\nishto'si me dridhamiti tato vakshyaami te hitam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Listen thou again to My supreme word, most secret of all; beloved art thou of Me, and steadfast of heart, therefore will I speak for thy benefit.","en2":"Hear thou again My supreme word, the profoundest of all; because thou art dearly beloved of Me, therefore will I speak what is good to thee.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":65,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि सत्यं ते प्रतिजाने प्रियोऽसि मे ॥","iast":"manmanā bhava madbhakto madyājī māṃ namaskuru |\nmāmevaiṣyasi satyaṃ te pratijāne priyo’si me ||","read":"manmanaa bhava madbhakto madyaajee maam namaskuru |\nmaamevaishyasi satyam te pratijaane priyo'si me ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Merge thy mind in Me, be my devotee, sacrifice to Me, prostrate thyself before Me, thou shalt come even to Me. I pledge thee My troth; thou art dear to Me.","en2":"Occupy thy mind with Me, be devoted to Me, sacrifice to Me, bow down to Me. Thou shalt reach Myself; truly do I promise unto thee, (for) thou art dear to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":66,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वधर्मान्परित्यज्य मामेकं शरणं व्रज ।\nअहं त्वा सर्वपापेभ्यो मोक्षयिष्यामि मा शुचः ॥","iast":"sarvadharmānparityajya māmekaṃ śaraṇaṃ vraja |\nahaṃ tvā sarvapāpebhyo mokṣayiṣyāmi mā śucaḥ ||","read":"sarvadharmaanparityajya maamekam sharanam vraja |\naham tvaa sarvapaapebhyo mokshayishyaami maa shuchah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Abandoning all duties come unto Me alone for shelter; sorrow not, I will liberate thee from all sins.","en2":"Relinquishing all Dharmas take refuge in Me alone; I will liberate thee from all sins; grieve not.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":67,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इदं ते नातपस्काय नाभक्ताय कदाचन ।\nन चाशुश्रूषवे वाच्यं न च मां योऽभ्यसूयति ॥","iast":"idaṃ te nātapaskāya nābhaktāya kadācana |\nna cāśuśrūṣave vācyaṃ na ca māṃ yo’bhyasūyati ||","read":"idam te naatapaskaaya naabhaktaaya kadaachana |\nna chaashushrooshave vaachyam na cha maam yo'bhyasooyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Never is this to be spoken by thee to anyone who is without asceticism, nor without devotion, nor to one who desireth not to listen, nor yet to him who speaketh evil of Me.","en2":"This is never to be spoken by thee to one who is devoid of austerities or devotion, nor to one who does not render service, nor to one who cavils at Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":68,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"य इमं परमं गुह्यं मद्भक्तेष्वभिधास्यति ।\nभक्तिं मयि परां कृत्वा मामेवैष्यत्यसंशयः ॥","iast":"ya imaṃ paramaṃ guhyaṃ madbhakteṣvabhidhāsyati |\nbhaktiṃ mayi parāṃ kṛtvā māmevaiṣyatyasaṃśayaḥ ||","read":"ya imam paramam guhyam madbhakteshvabhidhaasyati |\nbhaktim mayi paraam kritvaa maamevaishyatyasamshayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who shall declare this supreme secret among My devotees, having shown the highest devotion for Me, without doubt he shall come to Me.","en2":"He who with supreme devotion to Me will teach this deeply profound philosophy to My devotees, shall doubtless come to Me alone.","en2r":null,"rv":"Editions differ here (imaṃ / idaṃ); this is the vulgate reading.","kid":null},{"v":69,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न च तस्मान्मनुष्येषु कश्चिन्मे प्रियकृत्तमः ।\nभविता न च मे तस्मादन्यः प्रियतरो भुवि ॥","iast":"na ca tasmānmanuṣyeṣu kaścinme priyakṛttamaḥ |\nbhavitā na ca me tasmādanyaḥ priyataro bhuvi ||","read":"na cha tasmaanmanushyeshu kashchinme priyakrittamah |\nbhavitaa na cha me tasmaadanyah priyataro bhuvi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor is there any among men who performeth dearer service to Me than he, nor any other shall be more beloved by Me on earth than he.","en2":"Nor among men is there any who does dearer service to Me, nor shall there be another on earth dearer to Me, than he.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":70,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अध्येष्यते च य इमं धर्म्यं संवादमावयोः ।\nज्ञानयज्ञेन तेनाहमिष्टः स्यामिति मे मतिः ॥","iast":"adhyeṣyate ca ya imaṃ dharmyaṃ saṃvādamāvayoḥ |\njñānayajñena tenāhamiṣṭaḥ syāmiti me matiḥ ||","read":"adhyeshyate cha ya imam dharmyam samvaadamaavayoh |\njnaanayajnena tenaahamishtah syaamiti me matih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And he who shall study this sacred dialogue of ours, by him I shall be worshipped with the sacrifice of wisdom. Such is My mind.","en2":"And he who will study this sacred dialogue of ours, by him shall I have been worshipped by the Yajna of knowledge; such is My conviction.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":71,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च शृणुयादपि यो नरः ।\nसोऽपि मुक्तः शुभाँल्लोकान्प्राप्नुयात्पुण्यकर्मणाम् ॥","iast":"śraddhāvānanasūyaśca śṛṇuyādapi yo naraḥ |\nso’pi muktaḥ śubhām̐llokānprāpnuyātpuṇyakarmaṇām ||","read":"shraddhaavaananasooyashcha shrinuyaadapi yo narah |\nso'pi muktah shubhaanllokaanpraapnuyaatpunyakarmanaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The man also who, full of faith, merely heareth it unreviling, even he, freed from evil, obtaineth the radiant worlds of the righteous.","en2":"And even that man who hears this, full of Shraddhâ and free from malice, he too, liberated, shall attain to the happy worlds of those of righteous deeds.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":72,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कच्चिदेतच्छ्रुतं पार्थ त्वयैकाग्रेण चेतसा ।\nकच्चिदज्ञानसंमोहः प्रनष्टस्ते धनञ्जय ॥","iast":"kaccidetacchrutaṃ pārtha tvayaikāgreṇa cetasā |\nkaccidajñānasaṃmohaḥ pranaṣṭaste dhanañjaya ||","read":"kachchidetachchhrutam paartha tvayaikaagrena chetasaa |\nkachchidajnaanasammohah pranashtaste dhananjaya ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Hath this been heard, O son of Prithâ, with one-pointed mind? Has thy delusion, caused by unwisdom, been destroyed, O Dhananjaya?","en2":"Has this been heard by thee, Pârtha, with an attentive mind? Has the delusion of thy ignorance been destroyed, O Dhananjaya?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":73,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"नष्टो मोहः स्मृतिर्लब्धा त्वत्प्रसादान्मयाच्युत ।\nस्थितोऽस्मि गतसन्देहः करिष्ये वचनं तव ॥","iast":"naṣṭo mohaḥ smṛtirlabdhā tvatprasādānmayācyuta |\nsthito’smi gatasandehaḥ kariṣye vacanaṃ tava ||","read":"nashto mohah smritirlabdhaa tvatprasaadaanmayaachyuta |\nsthito'smi gatasandehah karishye vachanam tava ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Destroyed is my delusion. I have gained knowledge through Thy grace, O Immutable one. I am firm, my doubts have fled away. I will do according to Thy word.","en2":"Destroyed is my delusion, and I have gained my memory through Thy grace, O Achyuta. I am firm; my doubts are gone. I will do Thy word.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":74,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":"सञ्जय उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"इत्यहं वासुदेवस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः ।\nसंवादमिममश्रौषमद्भुतं रोमहर्षणम् ॥","iast":"ityahaṃ vāsudevasya pārthasya ca mahātmanaḥ |\nsaṃvādamimamaśrauṣamadbhutaṃ romaharṣaṇam ||","read":"ityaham vaasudevasya paarthasya cha mahaatmanah |\nsamvaadamimamashraushamadbhutam romaharshanam ||","spli":"sañjaya uvāca","splr":"sanjaya uvaacha","en":"Sanjaya said: I heard this marvellous dialogue of Vâsudeva, and of the great-souled Partha, causing my hair to stand on end.","en2":"Thus have I heard this wonderful dialogue between Vâsudeva and the high-souled Pârtha, causing my hair to stand on end.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":75,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"व्यासप्रसादाच्छ्रुतवानेतद्गुह्यमहं परम् ।\nयोगं योगेश्वरात्कृष्णात्साक्षात्कथयतः स्वयम् ॥","iast":"vyāsaprasādācchrutavānetadguhyamahaṃ param |\nyogaṃ yogeśvarātkṛṣṇātsākṣātkathayataḥ svayam ||","read":"vyaasaprasaadaachchhrutavaanetadguhyamaham param |\nyogam yogeshvaraatkrishnaatsaakshaatkathayatah svayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"By the favour of Vyâsa I listened to this secret and supreme yoga from the Lord of Yoga, Krishna Himself, speaking before mine eyes.","en2":"Through the grace of Vyâsa have I heard this supreme and most profound Yoga, direct from Krishna, the Lord of Yoga, Himself declaring it.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":76,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"राजन्संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य संवादमिममद्भुतम् ।\nकेशवार्जुनयोः पुण्यं हृष्यामि च मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","iast":"rājansaṃsmṛtya saṃsmṛtya saṃvādamimamadbhutam |\nkeśavārjunayoḥ puṇyaṃ hṛṣyāmi ca muhurmuhuḥ ||","read":"raajansamsmritya samsmritya samvaadamimamadbhutam |\nkeshavaarjunayoh punyam hrishyaami cha muhurmuhuh ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"O King, remembering, remembering this marvellous and holy dialogue between Keshava and Arjuna, I rejoice again and again.","en2":"O King, as I remember and remember this wonderful and holy dialogue between Keshava and Arjuna, I rejoice again and again.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":77,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तच्च संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य रूपमत्यद्भुतं हरेः ।\nविस्मयो मे महान् राजन् हृष्यामि च पुनः पुनः ॥","iast":"tacca saṃsmṛtya saṃsmṛtya rūpamatyadbhutaṃ hareḥ |\nvismayo me mahān rājan hṛṣyāmi ca punaḥ punaḥ ||","read":"tachcha samsmritya samsmritya roopamatyadbhutam hareh |\nvismayo me mahaan raajan hrishyaami cha punah punah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Remembering, remembering, also that most marvellous form of Hari, great is my wonder, O King. I rejoice, again and again.","en2":"And as I remember and remember that most wonderful Form of Hari, great is my wonder, O King; and I rejoice again and again.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":78,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्र योगेश्वरः कृष्णो यत्र पार्थो धनुर्धरः ।\nतत्र श्रीर्विजयो भूतिर्ध्रुवा नीतिर्मतिर्मम ॥","iast":"yatra yogeśvaraḥ kṛṣṇo yatra pārtho dhanurdharaḥ |\ntatra śrīrvijayo bhūtirdhruvā nītirmatirmama ||","read":"yatra yogeshvarah krishno yatra paartho dhanurdharah |\ntatra shreervijayo bhootirdhruvaa neetirmatirmama ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Wherever is Krishna, Yoga's Lord, wherever is Pârtha, the archer, assured are there prosperity, victory and happiness. So I think.","en2":"Wherever is Krishna, the Lord of Yoga, wherever is Pârtha, the wielder of the bow, there are prosperity, victory, expansion, and sound policy: such is my conviction.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null}];
